\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Pruning without a game. One informed trader facing a fixed price rule ($I=1$, no memory, $3\times 10^5$ periods, 100 runs per point, 95\% CIs). (a) With $\gamma =0$, standard Q-learning under-trades by about $0.91\sqrt  \alpha $ (dashed); counterfactual updates learn the optimal order at every step size. (b) At $\alpha =0.15$ the shortfall shrinks as the discount factor rises.}}{8}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{2}{8}{Pruning without a game. One informed trader facing a fixed price rule ($I=1$, no memory, $3\times 10^5$ periods, 100 runs per point, 95\% CIs). (a) With $\gamma =0$, standard Q-learning under-trades by about $\MechSqrtCoef \sqrt \alpha $ (dashed); counterfactual updates learn the optimal order at every step size. (b) At $\alpha =0.15$ the shortfall shrinks as the discount factor rises}{figure.caption.19}{}}
